@startuml
' Figure - Activity Diagram with partitions: registering evidence
!include _header.txt

|Investigator|
start
:Choose investigation and submit content;

|Interface Layer|
:Check the account's function;
if (entitled to register?) then (no)
  :Refuse with an explanation;
  |Audit|
  :Record the refusal;
  stop
else (yes)
endif

|Validation|
:Check the declared kind
against the content itself;
if (content matches its declared kind?) then (no)
  :Refuse the upload;
  |Audit|
  :Record the refusal;
  stop
else (yes)
endif

|Application Logic|
:Derive the content fingerprint;
:Extract embedded metadata;
:Encrypt the content for storage;

|Persistence|
fork
  :Write the evidence record;
fork again
  :Write the first custody record
  carrying the same fingerprint;
end fork
note right
  One indivisible operation. No evidence
  item can exist without a custody history
  (SR-12, DR-01).
end note
:Commit;

|Audit|
:Record the registration;

|Investigator|
:Show the registered item
with its fingerprint;
stop
@enduml
